The review has been written to `/Users/rich/source/HARES/docs/reviews/envelope/envelope-10-steady-state-init-zone-pinning.md`.

**Summary**: 3 findings — 1 Medium, 2 Low.

The key finding (Medium) is that `initialize_steady_state` has no defense-in-depth guard against zero-capacitance zones: while the standard construction pipeline clamps zone capacitance to ≥ 1,000 J/K, the initialization function itself never checks `wiring.c_zone_j_k` or `wiring.node_capacitances`. If a zero-capacitance zone were to reach it through a non-standard path, the singular reduced-matrix fallback silently fills all wall-mass state entries with `indoor_temp_c` — physically wrong and undiagnosed. By contrast, OCHRE's equivalent would raise `LinAlgError` via `np.linalg.inv`, failing loudly.
